  "id": "DrugBank_DB09054 - MONDO_2083",
  "verbalization": "Idelalisib, a phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI3K) inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia (ALL), with evidence linking it to the progression of the disease through interactions with other therapies like Venetoclax and Ofatumumab. The visible evidence suggests that Idelalisib may contribute to the development of Richter Syndrome, a severe and aggressive form of ALL characterized by the transformation of lymphoblastic leukemia into a more aggressive, non-lymphoblastic subtype. This is supported by the shared indication of ALL in all three paths, indicating a potential role of Idelalisib in the pathogenesis of this condition. The mechanism of action likely involves the inhibition of PI3K, which is frequently dysregulated in ALL, and may interact with other therapeutic agents to drive disease progression. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a plausible, though not yet fully understood, mechanistic link between Idelalisib and Richter Syndrome, particularly in the context of the disease’s progression and treatment resistance.",
